WEBVTT

00:01:36.721 --> 00:01:38.431
Game and match, Tezuka.

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.266
Six games to four.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.731
You want to go to Germany, don't you?

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:50.360
Go and become a professional already.

00:01:51.236 --> 00:01:52.153
Atobe.

00:01:52.821 --> 00:01:54.489
There's nothing for you to say, Tezuka.

00:01:56.574 --> 00:01:59.411
Just leave this team to me.

00:02:04.874 --> 00:02:07.627
Two wins and one loss.
We're finally ahead.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.170
Let's do this.

00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:19.222
"Promise"

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.061
Never thought we'd be playing

00:02:25.061 --> 00:02:27.981
against our seniors from Shishigaku

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:30.859
in a place like this, huh, Kippei?

00:02:30.859 --> 00:02:31.943
Yeah.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:36.114
Have you guys gotten any better?

00:02:36.114 --> 00:02:38.491
I'm going to enjoy this.

00:02:39.951 --> 00:02:41.995
You're leaving now?

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:42.996
Yes.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:45.373
But you haven't told Oishi or Momo.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:47.709
I'm sorry.

00:02:48.126 --> 00:02:50.211
At least let us send
you off with a party.

00:02:50.211 --> 00:02:51.129
Tezuka.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:56.217
I have a favor to ask of you.

00:03:07.228 --> 00:03:08.646
It disappeared.

00:03:09.314 --> 00:03:12.025
It's my Kamikakushi, Shun-<i>senpai</i>.

00:03:12.359 --> 00:03:13.902
What're you looking at, Shun?

00:03:13.902 --> 00:03:14.903
It's over here.

00:03:17.655 --> 00:03:18.990
Abare Dama!

00:03:20.992 --> 00:03:21.868
What?

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:25.080
Game, Tachibana-Chitose.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.498
Three games all.

00:03:28.124 --> 00:03:30.210
Shots that make the ball suddenly rise

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:32.337
and disappear from their
opponents' field of vision...

00:03:32.337 --> 00:03:35.965
and knuckle balls that make
the ball appear to multiply.

00:03:36.466 --> 00:03:40.637
They're not doing badly
against Shun and Washio.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:48.937
You guys play some good tennis.

00:03:48.937 --> 00:03:53.566
But you're still not a doubles team.

00:04:00.532 --> 00:04:01.574
That's...

00:04:02.617 --> 00:04:03.868
Synchronization.

00:04:06.162 --> 00:04:08.331
Now this is surprising.

00:04:08.331 --> 00:04:10.417
We shouldn't have expected
less from high schoolers.

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:14.295
I couldn't ask for more.

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:27.225
Why, Fuji?

00:04:27.809 --> 00:04:29.394
What's the point of this match?

00:04:32.731 --> 00:04:35.191
You can't beat Tezuka now.

00:04:51.916 --> 00:04:56.504
Tezuka, you're always
one step ahead of me.

00:04:59.924 --> 00:05:01.092
Fuji.

00:05:08.058 --> 00:05:10.310
Someday, I'll...

00:05:16.274 --> 00:05:19.402
I will surpass you.

00:05:23.782 --> 00:05:26.868
Game and match, team Suzuki-Washio.

00:05:26.868 --> 00:05:28.912
Seven games to six.

00:05:31.581 --> 00:05:34.125
The Two Wings of Kyushu lost.

00:05:34.542 --> 00:05:39.798
All the Court 3 players
are incredibly skilled.

00:05:40.757 --> 00:05:41.841
Good work.

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:42.717
Thanks.

00:05:43.802 --> 00:05:46.888
But it was a close match.

00:05:47.514 --> 00:05:50.934
They had a fierce final push.

00:05:52.143 --> 00:05:53.144
Sorry.

00:05:53.603 --> 00:05:55.563
Don't worry about it.

00:05:55.563 --> 00:05:59.067
You almost had them.
You scared them good.

00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:01.945
What's the point of scaring
someone if you can't beat them?

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:03.154
What?

00:06:03.822 --> 00:06:07.826
Your challenge was foolhardy.

00:06:07.826 --> 00:06:09.744
You're just a bunch of middle schoolers.

00:06:09.744 --> 00:06:14.332
I still can't believe you
made your way up to Court 5.

00:06:14.624 --> 00:06:15.792
What'd you say?

00:06:15.792 --> 00:06:17.127
Don't lose your cool.

00:06:20.296 --> 00:06:22.799
What are we here for?

00:06:24.092 --> 00:06:25.635
We're here to win.

00:06:30.765 --> 00:06:33.643
Hyotei will win! Atobe will win!

00:06:34.102 --> 00:06:37.772
Hyotei will win! Atobe will win!

00:06:37.772 --> 00:06:38.857
That's right.

00:06:38.857 --> 00:06:40.817
No matter what anyone says,

00:06:40.817 --> 00:06:43.278
if we take this next match, we'll win.

00:06:43.945 --> 00:06:47.240
Hyotei will win! Atobe will win!

00:06:47.574 --> 00:06:51.161
Hyotei will win! Atobe will win!

00:06:51.453 --> 00:07:06.593
Hyotei will win! Atobe will win!

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:11.514
The winner will be...

00:07:13.099 --> 00:07:14.684
Court 5!

00:07:16.811 --> 00:07:20.607
Is it true Court 5 might beat Court 3?

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:22.817
We'll have to see.

00:07:22.817 --> 00:07:24.944
However, I can tell you

00:07:24.944 --> 00:07:27.614
they've been evenly matched so far.

00:07:27.614 --> 00:07:29.449
Court 5's been completely taken over

00:07:29.449 --> 00:07:33.703
by middle schoolers,
with the exception of Oni.

00:07:34.412 --> 00:07:37.332
They're ridiculous.

00:07:37.332 --> 00:07:42.003
But, Coach Tsuge,
the speed of their improvement

00:07:42.003 --> 00:07:45.131
has surprised you more than
anyone else, hasn't it?

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:48.718
That's true, but...

00:07:49.344 --> 00:07:52.138
That Atobe stands out from the rest.

00:07:52.639 --> 00:07:55.225
His growth has been unbelievable.

00:07:56.351 --> 00:07:59.813
To be honest, I didn't think
you'd make it this far.

00:08:00.397 --> 00:08:02.982
Middle schoolers these days
are certainly impressive.

00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:06.236
However, like I told you before,

00:08:06.236 --> 00:08:10.407
you're not ready to aim for the top yet.

00:08:10.407 --> 00:08:13.201
I'm sick of hearing that.

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:22.544
One set match.

00:08:22.544 --> 00:08:24.254
Irie to serve.

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:29.843
I'm terrified.

00:08:32.012 --> 00:08:35.432
I can't believe how calm I am.

00:08:36.975 --> 00:08:38.309
That's a cross.

00:08:38.309 --> 00:08:41.688
You're getting ahead of yourself, moron!

00:08:45.025 --> 00:08:46.860
He hit a straight shot from that position.

00:08:48.361 --> 00:08:51.114
Your wrists shouldn't be that strong.

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:01.416
I evolve every day.

00:09:02.083 --> 00:09:04.210
It's the Rondo Towards Destruction.

00:09:04.627 --> 00:09:06.629
No, it's a feint.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:08.673
Drop shot.

00:09:10.008 --> 00:09:11.092
See?

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:14.429
I told you, you're getting
ahead of yourself.

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:17.432
It's obvious!

00:09:20.643 --> 00:09:22.937
I will show you how I've evolved.

00:09:43.541 --> 00:09:45.752
"Fugue Towards Disappointment."

00:09:54.928 --> 00:09:57.305
I-It can't be.

00:09:59.057 --> 00:10:01.518
I can't believe Irie is...

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:08.483
Game, Atobe.

00:10:08.483 --> 00:10:09.859
Five games to love.

00:10:11.027 --> 00:10:13.446
H-How?

00:10:16.199 --> 00:10:18.159
Impossible!

00:10:22.706 --> 00:10:23.873
I don't believe it.

00:10:23.873 --> 00:10:26.459
I can't believe I'm losing
to a middle schooler.

00:10:28.628 --> 00:10:30.839
If you're worried about high school

00:10:30.839 --> 00:10:33.633
or middle school, you're already finished!

00:10:34.259 --> 00:10:36.553
Tennis is simply about strong or weak.

00:10:36.553 --> 00:10:38.138
That's all!

00:10:38.471 --> 00:10:42.559
Atobe! Atobe!

00:10:42.559 --> 00:10:44.728
When this camp started,

00:10:44.728 --> 00:10:47.313
you may have been stronger than me.

00:10:48.815 --> 00:10:51.568
But that's in the distant past.

00:10:53.528 --> 00:10:57.198
I evolve faster every day!

00:10:57.490 --> 00:11:01.119
Like hell you will!

00:11:03.705 --> 00:11:05.165
It's over.

00:11:05.165 --> 00:11:09.377
I can see all your blind
spots with my insight.

00:11:10.295 --> 00:11:12.339
Now... Freeze!

00:11:16.551 --> 00:11:19.304
What? He has no blind spots?

00:11:20.555 --> 00:11:21.806
That bastard.

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:25.643
Was that all an act?

00:11:35.862 --> 00:11:37.947
You noticed?

00:11:45.663 --> 00:11:48.333
Was that all an act?

00:11:51.169 --> 00:11:52.337
Game, Irie.

00:11:52.337 --> 00:11:53.922
Two games to five.

00:11:54.631 --> 00:11:55.965
Game, Irie.

00:11:55.965 --> 00:11:57.509
Three games to five.

00:11:58.093 --> 00:12:02.764
Atobe-<i>san</i>'s getting destroyed now.

00:12:03.139 --> 00:12:07.435
That Irie's a trickster.

00:12:08.353 --> 00:12:10.855
He played me for a fool.

00:12:13.191 --> 00:12:14.484
Game, Irie.

00:12:14.484 --> 00:12:16.236
Four games to five.

00:12:16.236 --> 00:12:17.612
Come on, Atobe-<i>kun</i>.

00:12:17.612 --> 00:12:18.697
You can do it.

00:12:19.739 --> 00:12:21.157
Bastard.

00:12:22.409 --> 00:12:26.287
I'd hate to play against Irie.

00:12:26.621 --> 00:12:30.667
That high schooler's movements
completely changed.

00:12:31.292 --> 00:12:34.087
What's his deal?

00:12:34.587 --> 00:12:36.840
Irie doesn't belong on Court 3.

00:12:38.717 --> 00:12:42.929
I didn't mention it,
but he's much stronger.

00:12:46.307 --> 00:12:51.438
They put him on Court 3 to
raise the bar for all courts.

00:12:51.438 --> 00:12:54.232
Then we might be in trouble.

00:12:54.899 --> 00:12:56.776
You can do it!

00:12:56.776 --> 00:12:58.528
You can do it, Atobe-<i>san</i>!

00:12:58.778 --> 00:13:00.238
Shut up, Kirihara!

00:13:01.239 --> 00:13:03.199
Just shut up!

00:13:04.034 --> 00:13:05.410
That's right.

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:07.704
You must be embarrassed.

00:13:08.288 --> 00:13:10.749
You're wide open, Irie-<i>san</i>.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:13.918
Now... Freeze!

00:13:16.212 --> 00:13:20.133
I'll find your blind spots this time.

00:13:24.262 --> 00:13:27.557
In my court? But, how?

00:13:29.142 --> 00:13:34.147
Irie's strength is his ability
to read his opponent's emotions.

00:13:34.773 --> 00:13:40.362
He sees right through all
their thoughts and movements.

00:13:42.864 --> 00:13:44.032
Game, Irie.

00:13:44.032 --> 00:13:45.742
Six games to five.

00:13:46.576 --> 00:13:50.163
You're the one who's
wide open, Atobe-<i>kun</i>.

00:13:56.044 --> 00:13:59.547
I lived in England when I was a kid.

00:14:00.382 --> 00:14:02.008
He's Japanese.

00:14:02.008 --> 00:14:03.009
So poor.

00:14:03.009 --> 00:14:07.263
I know your way of tennis like
the palm of my hand, stupid.

00:14:07.764 --> 00:14:09.724
Even though they were my age,

00:14:09.724 --> 00:14:12.394
they were so much better
at tennis than me.

00:14:13.395 --> 00:14:15.855
They knew all my tricks and strategies.

00:14:15.855 --> 00:14:20.777
Faced with adversity that wouldn't
allow me to win, I honed one skill.

00:14:20.777 --> 00:14:22.445
The ability to find and mercilessly

00:14:22.445 --> 00:14:24.489
attack my opponent's weaknesses.

00:14:29.494 --> 00:14:32.038
No matter what anyone said,

00:14:32.539 --> 00:14:35.917
that was the only way for me.

00:14:42.298 --> 00:14:44.342
I-It's snowing.

00:14:48.179 --> 00:14:50.181
It seems...

00:14:51.224 --> 00:14:53.101
That's all I have.

00:14:54.185 --> 00:14:57.022
Looks like you're ready to play.

00:15:13.455 --> 00:15:15.957
Open all your pores.

00:15:15.957 --> 00:15:18.752
Push your nerves to their limits.

00:15:21.254 --> 00:15:23.006
Give up already.

00:15:23.423 --> 00:15:27.344
Why don't you abandon what's left
of your pride and admit defeat?

00:15:28.928 --> 00:15:30.305
Pride?

00:15:30.305 --> 00:15:32.390
That's got nothing to do with this!

00:15:32.390 --> 00:15:34.267
I'm doing this for the team!

00:15:34.559 --> 00:15:37.812
Now, where are your blind spots?

00:15:43.651 --> 00:15:45.653
I told you before the match.

00:15:47.238 --> 00:15:49.908
You're not ready for this yet.

00:15:55.038 --> 00:15:57.665
What? I can't see his blind spots.

00:16:01.002 --> 00:16:05.048
I will seize victory
through my own means...

00:16:05.048 --> 00:16:07.717
Using my insight!

00:16:10.261 --> 00:16:13.723
I can see right through you!

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:20.313
I couldn't... move.

00:16:23.983 --> 00:16:25.902
"Atobe Kingdom."

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:38.081
I can see them all too clearly.

00:16:38.081 --> 00:16:40.333
I can see your absolute blind spots.

00:16:40.834 --> 00:16:42.794
No matter how hard you try to hide them,

00:16:42.794 --> 00:16:47.007
your joints and bone structure
will tell me where they are.

00:16:47.841 --> 00:16:52.429
If I aim for your "absolute blind spots,"
where your body can't react,

00:16:53.596 --> 00:16:56.349
you won't even be able
to move to stop me.

00:16:57.058 --> 00:17:00.020
This is my world.

00:17:00.311 --> 00:17:01.938
My Atobe Kingdom!

00:17:02.439 --> 00:17:03.815
Game, Atobe.

00:17:03.815 --> 00:17:05.275
Six games all.

00:17:12.782 --> 00:17:13.992
I see.

00:17:14.576 --> 00:17:16.619
You've mastered your insight.

00:17:18.329 --> 00:17:21.041
You're unbelievable.

00:17:21.791 --> 00:17:23.001
All right.

00:17:23.001 --> 00:17:24.919
He's brought it to a tie breaker.

00:17:25.337 --> 00:17:27.839
Drawn out battles are
Atobe-<i>san</i>'s specialty.

00:17:31.843 --> 00:17:34.596
Your left ankle hurts, doesn't it?

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:38.850
Let's go.

00:17:40.018 --> 00:17:41.936
I'll give you your long battle.

00:17:49.444 --> 00:17:52.864
He's been running him around the court.

00:17:53.156 --> 00:17:56.534
He's going for that left ankle.

00:17:57.369 --> 00:17:59.162
This is pathetic.

00:17:59.996 --> 00:18:02.207
I've beaten countless opponents

00:18:02.207 --> 00:18:04.501
by attacking their
weaknesses in long battles.

00:18:05.335 --> 00:18:08.463
I never thought the same strategy
would be used against me.

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:10.882
Come on, it's up front next.

00:18:11.549 --> 00:18:13.301
How ironic.

00:18:15.762 --> 00:18:17.889
Are you all right? Does it hurt?

00:18:19.641 --> 00:18:22.227
You're an annoying bastard!

00:18:22.727 --> 00:18:23.728
Yes, yes.

00:18:23.728 --> 00:18:26.314
Now, go get it.

00:18:29.317 --> 00:18:30.110
Bastard.

00:18:31.778 --> 00:18:35.115
A long battle's exactly what I want!

00:18:43.748 --> 00:18:45.417
187.

00:18:45.417 --> 00:18:47.877
187, Atobe.

00:18:50.338 --> 00:18:51.840
Unbelievable.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:55.260
How is this tie breaker going on so long?

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:56.636
Why?

00:18:56.636 --> 00:19:00.640
What drives you so hard, Atobe-<i>kun</i>?

00:19:08.273 --> 00:19:09.399
Atobe.

00:19:10.483 --> 00:19:11.818
Tezuka...

00:19:12.318 --> 00:19:17.824
Has the pillar you tried to
carry always been this heavy?

00:19:21.578 --> 00:19:23.788
Now it's over!

00:19:25.165 --> 00:19:26.583
It's over!

00:19:28.001 --> 00:19:29.586
It's over!

00:19:31.671 --> 00:19:34.257
I said it's over!

00:19:34.257 --> 00:19:37.677
That's some great acting!

00:19:38.511 --> 00:19:40.263
He read my drop shot.

00:19:40.764 --> 00:19:41.848
In that case...

00:19:53.693 --> 00:20:00.116
I'll keep my promise, Tezuka!

00:20:16.466 --> 00:20:17.634
Atobe!

00:20:17.634 --> 00:20:18.885
Atobe-<i>san</i>!

00:20:19.719 --> 00:20:22.806
What? It's over?

00:20:25.934 --> 00:20:30.230
Man, I'm impressed.

00:20:31.731 --> 00:20:35.652
I can't lift my shoulder anymore.

00:20:37.028 --> 00:20:38.571
Nice fight.

00:20:40.699 --> 00:20:43.576
As neither player can continue playing,

00:20:43.576 --> 00:20:45.286
the match is abandoned.

00:20:48.707 --> 00:20:51.501
With the Court 3 versus
Court 5 team shuffle

00:20:51.501 --> 00:20:53.962
match score at two to two
and one abandoned match,

00:20:53.962 --> 00:20:56.506
the next singles match
will decide the winner.

00:20:57.757 --> 00:20:59.426
A tie breaker match?

00:21:01.469 --> 00:21:05.265
Send one representative
from each team to the court.

00:21:06.933 --> 00:21:08.184
Out of the way!

00:21:08.184 --> 00:21:09.519
I'll go.

00:21:14.774 --> 00:21:16.359
Sorry, sir.

00:21:16.818 --> 00:21:18.778
The snow's causing some delays.

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:20.572
Not at all.

00:21:20.572 --> 00:21:25.410
Because of it, I heard the
important yell of a friend.

00:23:17.230 --> 00:23:18.273
"Preview"

00:23:18.273 --> 00:23:20.608
"Preview"
Is this our final exam?

00:23:20.608 --> 00:23:22.402
This is the first step in our revolution.

00:23:22.402 --> 00:23:27.365
It's time to show those winners how
we've grown through our training.

00:23:27.365 --> 00:23:29.034
We can't let our guard down.

00:23:29.034 --> 00:23:32.829
That's right. We can't
afford any mistakes now.

00:23:32.829 --> 00:23:35.832
One misstep and it's all over.

00:23:35.832 --> 00:23:38.501
Let's go, everyone!

00:23:42.964 --> 00:23:44.424
"The Start of a Revolution"
The next episode of <i>Prince of</i>
<i>Tennis II </i>is: "The Start of a Revolution."

00:23:44.424 --> 00:23:47.307
"The Start of a Revolution"
Let's do this.
